Bug Report: Missing HDA quirk for Dell Precision 7550 (ALC289, SSID 1028:09=
c3)

Summary

Audible click/pop noise on internal speaker output at the start and
end of audio playback on a Dell Precision 7550. Confirmed absent on
Windows (same hardware, dual-boot), present only under Linux. The
codec falls back to a generic "pin match" fixup because there is no
dedicated quirk entry for this Dell subsystem ID in
sound/pci/hda/patch_realtek.c.

System information

Laptop model: Dell Precision 7550
Baseboard: 090NVT
Codec: Realtek ALC289
Codec Vendor ID: 0x10ec0289
Codec Subsystem ID: 0x102809c3 (PCI SSID: 1028:09c3, Dell)
Kernel version tested: 7.1.8-100.fc43.x86_64 and
7.1.10-100.fc43.x86_64 (issue persists on both)
Distro: Fedora 43
Audio stack: PipeWire 1.4.11 + WirePlumber 0.5.14

Steps already ruled out

The following were tested and confirmed NOT to be the cause:

snd_hda_intel power_save =E2=80=94 set to 0, no change
WirePlumber session.suspend-timeout-seconds =E2=80=94 set to 0 (confirmed v=
ia
wpctl inspect), no change
Continuous PCM keep-alive stream (verified actively running via ps
aux), no change
Latest available Fedora kernel (7.1.10-100.fc43) =E2=80=94 no change
Pin configuration via hdajackretask =E2=80=94 inspected, matches expected
standard layout (0x14 =3D Internal Speaker, 0x19 =3D Headset Mic), nothing
to override

dmesg evidence

[   11.076689] snd_hda_codec_alc269 hdaudioC0D0: ALC289: picked fixup
(pin match)
[   11.077250] snd_hda_codec_alc269 hdaudioC0D0: autoconfig for
ALC289: line_outs=3D1 (0x14/0x0/0x0/0x0/0x0) type:speaker
[   11.077252] snd_hda_codec_alc269 hdaudioC0D0:    speaker_outs=3D0
(0x0/0x0/0x0/0x0/0x0)
[   11.077254] snd_hda_codec_alc269 hdaudioC0D0:    hp_outs=3D1
(0x21/0x0/0x0/0x0/0x0)
[   11.077255] snd_hda_codec_alc269 hdaudioC0D0:    mono: mono_out=3D0x0
[   11.077256] snd_hda_codec_alc269 hdaudioC0D0:    inputs:
[   11.077257] snd_hda_codec_alc269 hdaudioC0D0:      Internal Mic=3D0x12
[   11.077258] snd_hda_codec_alc269 hdaudioC0D0:      Headset Mic=3D0x19
[   11.077259] snd_hda_codec_alc269 hdaudioC0D0:      Headphone Mic=3D0x1b

Note the empty fixup name =E2=80=94 this confirms no matching
SND_PCI_QUIRK(0x1028, 0x09c3, ...) entry currently exists for this
SSID in patch_realtek.c's ALC269/ALC289 quirk table.

Expected behavior

No click/pop should occur at playback start/stop, matching behavior
under Windows on identical hardware (dual-boot, same physical
machine).

Actual behavior

Audible tick/click heard at the beginning and end of every audio
playback through the internal speaker (pin 0x14). Not present through
the headphone jack in preliminary testing. Not tied to idle-suspend =E2=80=
=94
confirmed present even with idle-suspend fully disabled and a
continuous keep-alive stream active.

Requested fix

Addition of a SND_PCI_QUIRK(0x1028, 0x09c3, "Dell Precision 7550",
ALC289_FIXUP_DELL_...) entry to the ALC269/ALC289 quirk table in
sound/pci/hda/patch_realtek.c, similar to existing entries for other
Dell Precision/XPS models with the same ALC289 codec (e.g. Precision
5560, XPS models) that address analogous pop/click issues via
ALC289_FIXUP_DELL_SPK_LFE or similar existing quirk functions.

Attachments

Full codec dump: alc289_codec_dump.txt (attached separately)

